From bde12cd8671a6128c69ea92163b3a62442cb2b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:11:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 163/209] fix: the CineCam Grade preset slot no longer keeps a
 raw pointer to its component (S10 item 6)

Sandbox died with a heap corruption (0xC0000374) around the CineCam Grade
component's property data: four dumps on 2026-09-10, all on the main thread with
the render thread idle, three of them freeing a CryString in the grade panel's
idle poll and one in the inspector's Schematyc property snapshot. The freeing
site was never the writer.

Root cause, argued from the code (page heap could not be run, see below):

SCineGradePresetSlot is a REFLECTED type, and it held a raw
CCineGradeComponent* plus two Serialization::ActionButtons built with
functor(*this, &member). Both are pointers into a component, embedded in a value
that Schematyc and the editor copy, cache and outlive:

  * CClassProperties::Read copy-constructs the slot into a CScratchpad on every
    inspector widget build, and CEntityComponentsCache keeps one across a whole
    game-mode round trip;
  * CClassProperties::Apply copies that cached value back ONTO the live
    component - the pointer with it - and Apply also runs before Initialize();
  * PropertyRowActionButton clones the functor it is given and keeps the clone
    for the life of the row, which survives revert, game mode, undo and a level
    reload.

OnExport() then wrote through that pointer: SetAppliedPath() is two
CryStringT::operator=, i.e. a real CryModuleFree and a store. A free of a stale
block and a store into freed memory, with no symptom until some later, innocent
free - which is what the four dumps are.

The fix: the way back becomes an EntityId instead of a pointer. Serialize() and
both buttons resolve the component fresh on every use through
gEnv->pEntitySystem->GetEntity(id)->GetComponent<>() and never store the result,
and the buttons are lambdas capturing the id BY VALUE, so the row's cloned
functor owns nothing at all. EntityId carries a salt, so a stale id resolves to
nullptr rather than to a stranger's memory; copying, caching and Apply-ing the
struct become meaningless instead of dangerous. Item 4b's behaviour is
unchanged: the apply still happens inside the input serialization, so it is
still inside the editor's save snapshot (EntityObject.cpp:912 before :928), the
picker row still does apply()+revert() so the inspector redraws, and the undo
transaction still covers the whole component.

Containment, labelled as such: CineGradeBinding.cpp ReadOne/WriteOne now copy
characters instead of assigning CryStrings, so the panel no longer co-owns a
refcounted block with a component in another DLL and can no longer be the module
that frees it from an idle timer.

Everything else the integration audit listed as a candidate was read and
excluded - the .cube parser, the LUT wrap and upload, the texture release by
name, the curve bake, the panel's loops and raster, the asset sidecar writer,
and the Schematyc scratchpad's sizing. Notes in
scene-notes/research/s10-6-grade-heap-corruption.md, decision in
scene-notes/decisions/s10-grade-component.md section "Item 6".

Not confirmed by page heap: gflags is not installed, enabling page heap by hand
needs elevation, and the reproduction is a GUI sequence the editor automation
harness cannot drive. The WER dumps are minidumps and carry no heap pages, so
the corrupting pattern could not be read post-mortem either.

